Corresponding source
--------------------
Each distributed build corresponds to the exact commit named by its release tag
in the canonical repository https://github.com/Zeno-cc/FilmFrame. That commit
holds the complete corresponding source of the static application, the Access
service and the updater.

Build instructions for the corresponding source:

- static application: README.md, section 快速开始 (`npm ci`, `npm run build`).
- Access service: server/access/README.md (`npm ci`, `npm run build`).
- host updater: ops/updater/README.md.
- container images: built from the same commit by
  `.github/workflows/release.yml`; the build inputs are the repository itself.

Upstream works
--------------
- SpektraLab — https://github.com/JamesQiu2005/SpektraLab, pinned revision
  02d82b56cf65f0f8e802a708612edc4e9a4790af, GPL-3.0-or-later. C++/Metal film and
  print engine that the spectral pipeline, the physical 135 edge model and the
  product monochrome data were translated from. No SpektraLab name, icon, cover,
  font, artwork or endorsement is used.
- spektrafilm — https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm, pinned revision
  3bb2c2d2801ff68b92019cf1dbcbb133d60832bc, GPL-3.0-or-later with the measured
  profiles, LUTs and their direct derivatives under CC BY-SA 4.0. Film/paper
  process model and the measured film, paper and positive profiles that the
  shipped spectral stock data derives from. Both license texts are retained
  under ops/provenance/licenses/, and every modification or derivative is
  recorded in ops/provenance/PROFILE-CHANGELOG.md.
- Empty-darkroom documentary photographs are public-domain or CC-licensed works;
  per-image attribution and the asset provenance records live in
  docs/asset-sources/ and ops/provenance/licenses/.

